1
00:00:00,244 --> 00:00:03,118
Your iPhone has a button that can put its screen on your PC.

2
00:00:03,358 --> 00:00:04,675
Almost nobody uses it.

3
00:00:04,944 --> 00:00:05,578
No cable.

4
00:00:05,817 --> 00:00:06,863
No app on your phone.

5
00:00:07,102 --> 00:00:07,783
No account.

6
00:00:08,022 --> 00:00:08,915
No subscription.

7
00:00:09,094 --> 00:00:09,728
Just this.

8
00:00:10,544 --> 00:00:11,390
It’s called Mirlow.

9
00:00:12,594 --> 00:00:14,042
Open Mirlow on your PC.

10
00:00:14,144 --> 00:00:16,193
On your iPhone, tap Screen Mirroring.

11
00:00:16,256 --> 00:00:17,043
Pick your PC.

12
00:00:17,594 --> 00:00:18,204
And that’s it.

13
00:00:18,443 --> 00:00:19,254
Sound included.

14
00:00:20,744 --> 00:00:22,557
And here’s the part nobody expects.

15
00:00:22,844 --> 00:00:26,013
You can control your iPhone with your PC’s mouse and keyboard.

16
00:00:26,244 --> 00:00:26,654
Click.

17
00:00:26,893 --> 00:00:27,432
Scroll.

18
00:00:27,683 --> 00:00:28,081
Type.

19
00:00:28,694 --> 00:00:32,158
It pairs like a real Bluetooth mouse, so there’s almost no delay.

20
00:00:32,406 --> 00:00:37,191
Plus full screen, it stays private, and it works on iPhone, iPad and Android.

21
00:00:37,556 --> 00:00:38,484
So what’s the catch?

22
00:00:38,706 --> 00:00:39,387
There isn’t one.

23
00:00:39,626 --> 00:00:40,248
It’s free.

24
00:00:40,487 --> 00:00:43,455
No trial, no watermark, and it’s open source.

25
00:00:43,644 --> 00:00:44,384
Search Mirlow.

26
00:00:44,635 --> 00:00:45,351
Thank me later.
